WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.920
What a working engineer does with this.

2
00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:16.429
Before you give an agent a new tool, write one line for it in a table: read or write, reversible or not, which credential it uses and what that credential can reach, and what happens if it is called with the worst arguments you can imagine.

3
00:00:16.709 --> 00:00:22.555
Then choose the control per row: run freely, run in a sandbox, ask a human, or leave it out.

4
00:00:22.835 --> 00:00:24.669
Put the table in your design doc.

5
00:00:24.949 --> 00:00:32.416
It is the artifact a security reviewer will ask for, and it is the one you will use in the project to justify your design.
